  "reply_text": "Found **one merge-blocking bug**:\n\n**[P1] View-only shares can edit unlocked documents — `src/guard.js:12`**\n\n`share.mask & WRITE === WRITE` is parsed as `share.mask & (WRITE === WRITE)`, effectively checking `mask & 1`—the **READ** bit, not WRITE.\n\nConfirmed:\n- Viewer (`mask: 1`): `canEdit` returns **true**, incorrectly granting edit access.\n- WRITE-only share (`mask: 4`): returns **0**, incorrectly denying edit access.\n\nUse `hasRight(share.mask, WRITE)` or parenthesize the bitwise expression before comparing. Add negative coverage for a viewer editing an unlocked document; the existing editor test passes because editors also have READ.\n\nAll six existing tests pass, so they currently miss this authorization bug. No other concrete issues found in the diff. **No files changed.**",
